// Target-owned UEFI x86-64 OS-loader handoff contract.
//
// A bound OS loader reaches this surface to perform the nonreturning custody
// transfer out of Boot Services into the loaded OS entry. This is the authored
// invocation route for the runtime edge owned by `drive_uefi_os_handoff_cycle`:
// the generated adapter acquires explicit map-buffer storage, retains the
// allocation roster, Boot-Services identity, surviving-stack evidence, and
// remaining attempt bound, then drives the bounded GetMemoryMap/ExitBootServices
// retry ledger. A successful call never returns: Boot Services custody is
// consumed and control transfers to `entry`. When every bounded attempt is
// spent on a stale key the adapter performs the invocation's firmware return
// with the target-authored exhaustion status, so this contract carries no
// result on either branch.
//
// Like `UefiApplication`, this remains a planned, non-invoked surface until the
// settled bootstrap adapter and generated shell are built: the boundary machine
// below names the target's realization of the edge, and the generated custody
// transfer is the deferred emission. The surface alone establishes no Boot
// Services authority.

// The invocable nonreturning custody-transfer surface. `entry` is the exact
// loaded OS entry the adapter transfers control to after Boot Services are
// consumed; the OS entry's own calling contract is a separate boundary.
pub boundary trait UefiOsHandoff {
    machine handoff(entry: addr)
        reaches UefiOsHandoff;
}

// Nominal owner of the complete selected handoff provider closure. The
// boundary realization attaches to this type so provider selection never
// assembles the nonreturning edge from unrelated implementations.
pub data UefiOsHandoffNativeProvider { }

// The `boundary machine` supply is inferred from the exact realization symbol,
// normalized signature, package custody, and selected target; the realization
// is the runtime edge's generated custody transfer.
uefi_x86_64 boundary machine UefiOsHandoffNativeProvider::handoff(entry: addr)
    satisfies UefiOsHandoff::handoff;
